## 7. AI in Fetal Imaging

One of the important areas discussed in the paper is AI-assisted fetal ultrasound.

The review highlights AI systems that can assist with:

- fetal anomaly detection
- image analysis
- anatomical segmentation
- screening

For example, the paper discusses GE Voluson SWIFT as an AI-enhanced 3D ultrasound application for fetal anomaly detection.

The validation evidence summarized in the paper includes approximately 5,000 scans and reports 94% sensitivity for the cited example.

Samsung iNSIGHT is another example discussed for real-time segmentation and analysis of obstetric images.

The paper reports approximately 2,000 images and a Dice coefficient of 0.89 for the cited technical validation.

These examples demonstrate how AI can automate or assist with complex fetal imaging tasks.

