## 18. Workflow Integration

The paper emphasizes that AI should fit naturally into clinical workflows.

A model can have good predictive performance but still be difficult to use if:

- the output is difficult to understand
- it requires unnecessary manual steps
- it does not integrate with existing systems
- it increases workload

Therefore:

**Good model performance is not the same as complete clinical usefulness.**

A practical healthcare AI system should also be:

- understandable
- usable
- accessible
- workflow-compatible

This supports our plan to provide a user-facing system rather than only a machine-learning model.

