## 23. Five Practical Lessons from the Paper

The paper provides five important practical lessons about AI.

### 1. AI works best when the problem is specific

A clear and well-defined problem makes it easier to develop useful AI systems.

### 2. AI can reduce documentation burden

AI can help structure and summarize clinical information.

### 3. AI is strong at pattern recognition but does not replace clinical intuition

AI can identify patterns in data, but clinicians remain responsible for interpreting the broader clinical situation.

### 4. AI can help explain complex information

AI can assist with communicating complex medical information when the content is reviewed by clinicians.

### 5. AI can improve through structured feedback

The paper discusses feedback from clinicians as a way of improving AI systems over time.

These lessons reinforce the idea that healthcare AI should be developed as a human-AI collaboration.

